submission_format:
Return a JSON object with the same keys and nesting as the example below.

```json
{
  "artifacts": {
    "run_log": "/workspace/output/run.jsonl"
  },
  "results": {
    "beta": 0.0
  }
}
```

Units: beta in K^-1.

Use the format below for the file `/workspace/output/run.jsonl`:
JSONL, one record per production sample from each NPT heating stage between 300 and 500 K, including the additional stages around 400 K. Use distinct integer stage_index values, branch="heating", ensemble="NPT", and phase="production". Temperatures are K and volume is Angstrom^3.
```text
{"type":"sample","stage_index":0,"branch":"heating","ensemble":"NPT","target_temperature_K":300.0,"phase":"production","temperature_K":300.0,"volume_A3":1800.0}
```
